{
  "vcon": "0.4.0",
  "uuid": "385e0dfe-8313-8677-bc7d-24f3a5d50e3c",
  "created_at": "2026-01-21T14:19:58-05:00",
  "subject": "Inbound call, Public Works",
  "parties": [
    {
      "name": "Lucia Correia",
      "role": "resident",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    },
    {
      "name": "Lorraine Medeiros",
      "role": "clerk",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    }
  ],
  "dialog": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-21T14:17:20-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Public Works, this is Lorraine. How can I help you?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-21T14:17:24-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Hello, yes, good afternoon. I have a question about recycling, and also about my bin. Is this the right department?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-21T14:17:31-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "It is, yes. Go ahead, what's the question?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-21T14:17:35-05:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay. So, what can go in the recycling now? I want to check three things. Pizza boxes, glass, and the plastic clamshells, like from strawberries or salad."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-21T14:17:45-05:00",
      "duration": 17,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay, pizza boxes, glass, and clamshells. Let's take them one at a time. Pizza boxes are fine as long as they're not soaked through with grease. If the top is clean you can tear that part off and recycle it, and the greasy bottom goes in the trash."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-21T14:18:02-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "The top clean, the bottom greasy goes in trash. Okay. Thank you. And glass?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-21T14:18:08-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Glass bottles and jars are accepted. Empty them and give them a quick rinse, and lids can go back on."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-21T14:18:15-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Bottles and jars, rinse, lids on. Okay, good. And the clamshells?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-21T14:18:20-05:00",
      "duration": 15,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes, the clear plastic clamshell containers generally go in with the rest of the plastics, as long as they're empty and rinsed. If you're ever unsure about a certain number on the bottom, you can call back and we'll look it up for you."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-21T14:18:35-05:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay, clamshells yes, empty and rinsed. Thank you, thank you. Now, my bin. The lid is broken, it cracked in the cold. How do I request a replacement?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-21T14:18:45-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I can take that request right now. Is it the recycling bin or the trash barrel?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-21T14:18:51-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "The recycling bin. The blue one."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-21T14:18:54-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "The blue recycling bin, cracked lid. And what's the location?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-21T14:18:58-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "It's 207 Dixon Street. In the North End."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-21T14:19:02-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "207 Dixon Street. Is that right, Dixon with an X?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-21T14:19:06-05:00",
      "duration": 2,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes, D-I-X-O-N. Correct."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-21T14:19:08-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Got it. And can I get a name and a callback number in case the crew has a question?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-21T14:19:15-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Lucia Correia, C-O-R-R-E-I-A. The number is 401-555-0175."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-21T14:19:18-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Lucia Correia, 401-555-0175. Let me read it back. Blue recycling bin, broken lid, 207 Dixon Street. Is that everything?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-21T14:19:25-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes, that is right. Oh, sorry, I need to hurry a little. I have a parent-teacher conference at four, and I must leave soon."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-21T14:19:34-05:00",
      "duration": 12,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "No problem, we're just about done. The request is in. Replacement bins usually go out within a couple of weeks, but it can vary. Just leave the old one at the curb if they ask."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-21T14:19:46-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Leave the old one at the curb. Okay. Thank you very much, you were very helpful."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-21T14:19:52-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "You're welcome, Lucia. Good luck at the conference."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-21T14:19:56-05:00",
      "duration": 2,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Thank you. Goodbye."
    }
  ],
